                <pb facs="0502" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg422"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.01/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-01T18:00:00-05:00">July 1, 1930—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>51. Foreign Office informs me that Siles will arrive in Arica tomorrow afternoon
                    escorted by Brazilian Secretary and Chilean Military Attaché and that Chilean
                    Minister in La Paz has been instructed to express good will privately to the
                    junta, but recognition for the present is not contemplated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
